          <button class="btn-primary" onclick="next(['q2_1','q2_2','q2_3','q2_4','q2_5'],'s2-error','screen-s3')">Continue &#8594;</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- S3 -->
    <div class="screen" id="screen-s3">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="section-label">Section 3 of 7</div>
        <div class="section-title">Data Quality, Lineage &amp; Management</div>
        <div class="section-desc">Confirming that your AI systems are supported by clear, auditable data practices.</div>
        <div class="q-block">
          <div class="q-label"><span class="q-num">3.1</span>Is the origin and source of data used by AI systems documented and accessible?</div>
          <div class="q-hint">i.e. where data comes from, how it is collected and processed</div>
          <div class="options" id="q3_1">
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_1',3)"><span class="option-dot"></span>Fully documented</label>
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_1',1)"><span class="option-dot"></span>Partially documented</label>
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_1',0)"><span class="option-dot"></span>Not documented</label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="q-block">
          <div class="q-label"><span class="q-num">3.2</span>Do you maintain records of data lineage for core AI systems?</div>
          <div class="q-hint">Sources, transformations, and version history</div>
          <div class="options" id="q3_2">
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_2',3)"><span class="option-dot"></span>Yes, comprehensive records</label>
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_2',1)"><span class="option-dot"></span>Limited records exist</label>
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_2',0)"><span class="option-dot"></span>No</label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="q-block">
          <div class="q-label"><span class="q-num">3.3</span>Do you perform regular data quality assessments for inputs feeding AI decisions?</div>
          <div class="options" id="q3_3">
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_3',3)"><span class="option-dot"></span>Yes, on a scheduled basis</label>
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_3',1)"><span class="option-dot"></span>Yes, but ad-hoc only</label>
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_3',0)"><span class="option-dot"></span>No</label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="q-block">
          <div class="q-label"><span class="q-num">3.4</span>Is there a documented process for identifying and resolving data quality issues?</div>
          <div class="options" id="q3_4">
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_4',3)"><span class="option-dot"></span>Yes, formal documented process</label>
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_4',1)"><span class="option-dot"></span>Yes, but informal</label>
            <label class="option" onclick="pick(this,'q3_4',0)"><span class="option-dot"></span>No</label>
          </div>
        </div>
